From: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: add the RTL8221B HiSGMII entry

Register the board-specific RTL8221B match for the 2.5G port,
including the cold PHY initialization after the GPIO128 reset and the
vendor GPIO14 handoff that the generic entry omits.

The entry uses its own read_mmd/write_mmd so every devad is reached through
the IEEE 802.3 MMD indirect sequence (C22 0x0d/0x0e). Upstream's
rtl822xb_read_mmd() sends MDIO_MMD_VEND2 registers outside 0xA400..0xA43C
through the RTL821x page-select window instead, and that window does not
carry this part's SerDes block: reading 0x7580 as page 0x758 / offset 0x10
returns 0 where the MMD path returns 0x9412. With the page path the state
machine's read_status() times out (-110), phydev->link never becomes 1,
rtl_adjust_link() never calls phy_set_speed(), and the SoC S3 lane keeps
whatever the bootloader left behind, so the 2.5G jack never passes traffic.

Signed-off-by: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -3811,7 +3811,21 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+#include "rtl8221b-rtl9617c.h"
+
 static struct phy_driver realtek_drvs[] = {
+	{
+		.match_phy_device = rtl8221b_rtl9617c_match,
+		.name		= "RTL8221B HiSGMII PHY",
+		.get_features	= rtl8221b_rtl9617c_get_features,
+		.config_init	= rtl8221b_rtl9617c_config_init,
+		.config_aneg	= rtl8221b_rtl9617c_config_aneg,
+		.read_status	= rtl822x_c45_read_status,
+		.suspend	= genphy_c45_pma_suspend,
+		.resume		= rtl8221b_rtl9617c_resume,
+		.read_mmd	= rtl8221b_read_mmd,
+		.write_mmd	= rtl8221b_write_mmd,
+	},
 	{
 		PHY_ID_MATCH_EXACT(0x00008201),
 		.name		= "RTL8201CP Ethernet",
